{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>On the first of the month it shall be for you a rest.</b> When the first of the month is for you a rest, then it is זכרון תרועה (a remembrance of teru'ah) — that is to say, when Rosh HaShanah falls on Shabbat there is no teru'ah, as our Rabbis decreed, and there is only a mere remembrance of teru'ah. Therefore in the prayer of Rosh HaShanah that falls on Shabbat we say: ״this day of remembrance, a remembrance of teru'ah.״ And in the section of Pinchas it does not write שבתון but only ״a day of teru'ah it shall be for you״ — meaning, when it falls on a weekday, we say: ״this day of remembrance, a day of teru'ah.״ And so the liturgical poet composed in the Rosh HaShanah piyyut: If it occurs on holy Shabbat — ״a remembrance of teru'ah״ is its scriptural nature; if it comes on a weekday — ״you were commanded to sound the shofar throughout your borders,״ ״a day of teru'ah it shall be for you.״" "<b>A remembrance of teru'ah.</b> Through the teru'ah you will be remembered before HaKadosh Baruch Hu, as it is written: ״והרעותם ונזכרתם״ (and you shall sound and you shall be remembered)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:40.730400875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}